WEBVTT

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:11.110
The victor in the first match 
of the Autumn Elections is...

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:16.500
Candidate Yukihira Souma!

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.330
Glad you liked it!

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.580
He won!

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.580
Woohoo!

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.050
C'mon, don't cry like a kid just 
because you lost.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:28.800
Stand up.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:34.890
Thank—

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.690
Guess I'm now one step ahead of you

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.640
in the fight to become 
one of the next Elite Ten.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:39.990
What?!

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.900
Don't act all high and mighty
 just because you won!

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.690
Let me tell you something.
 This isn't the last you'll see of me!

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.650
I'm not going to let you have 
the top seat at Tohtsuki!

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:49.900
Have a good day, Yukihira-kun!

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.090
I guess your skills are not that impressive.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.500
What? What? What?!

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:04.650
I guess you're a genius not only at cooking but also at insults!

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.210
You do realize you're 
complimenting my cooking?

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.470
Listen!

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.680
Just wait till I get my revenge!

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:12.400
Stupid Erina!

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.260
I envy you.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:18.640
You can just cry like that whenever you want.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.270
Souma-kun.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.350
I was watching from the standby room.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:25.150
Congratulations!

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:27.990
Thanks, Tadokoro.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:29.370
It's your turn, huh?

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:30.820
You look pretty calm.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.380
Am I?

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:34.280
I guess so!

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:40.690
See, I could only think 
of trying my best in the prelims.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:45.050
But now, I'm hoping 
to enjoy my own cooking.

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:47.380
It's the first time I've felt this way!

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.530
I see.

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.760
Well, try not to get too tense.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:52.550
Good luck!

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:53.760
Thanks!

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.850
Your cooking's too pretty, as usual.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.370
Are you trying to lecture me?

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:05.350
Know your place.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:09.190
I believe I do know my place.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:13.150
Anyway, miss... you should save that line

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.820
for when you beat me in cooking.

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:20.210
Next is the second match in the first round!

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:21.540
The candidates are coming in!

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:30.420
Here is our dark horse candidate, Candidate Tadokoro Megumi,
 who passed the Block B preliminaries at the very last minute!

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.850
Good luck!

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.590
Her opponent is Candidate Kurokiba Ryou,

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:39.060
who was tied with Candidate Yukihira Souma for second place in the Block A preliminaries!

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:42.180
The theme...

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.060
is ramen!

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.420
Let the cooking begin!

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:17.670
Far beyond the image I have in my mind

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:24.140
The reality I'm building up is still far away

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.890
An endless journey

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:32.900
Let's hone each other's pride

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.400
Words aren't really important

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.900
So let's just say "yes" and leave it at that

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:44.870
We fight each other and hone our skills

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.750
Our encounters cause shockwaves

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.500
We're reckless challengers

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:57.500
Heading toward a world as yet unexplored

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.050
A swordsman should use his blade

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:02.880
To open the way to the future

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:08.600
This is my story and no one else's

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.870
That concludes the general overview.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:32.160
One last thing: we'll provide the noodles.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.020
The match is tomorrow, after all.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:37.670
We made the noodles 
in advance to let them rest.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:41.740
Choose which type of noodles you want before the day's end, and let us—

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.920
Flat/Wide Noodles

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.920
Flat/Wide Noodles

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:42.050
Egg Noodles

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:42.050
Egg Noodles

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:42.630
Thickness

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:42.630
Straight Noodles

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:42.630
Thickness

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:42.630
Straight Noodles

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:45.010
I'll choose this one from wide noodles.

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:47.020
Are you sure that's your final choice?

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.740
It'll be fine.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:52.360
I already know what kind 
of ramen I'll be making.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.280
<i>He figured that out just now?</i>

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.930
Tadokoro-chan, there's no need to rush.

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:01.450
You just need to tell us by midnight.

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.450
O-Okay.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.730
<i>Since the organizers will prepare the noodles,</i>

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:10.230
<i>maybe that means they want us 
to focus on the broth.</i>

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:16.930
<i>The broth is created by its base made of stock,
 the concentrated sauce known as kaeshi,</i>

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:19.670
<i>along with various 
infused oils and spices.</i>

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.930
<i>If those components fail to complement each other, 
the flavor will be fragmented.</i>

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:29.510
<i>The noodles Kurokiba-kun selected have an oval cross-section with a notable elasticity.</i>

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:33.850
<i>Wide noodles are typically paired 
with rich, strong flavors.</i>

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:38.860
<i>Maybe that means Kurokiba-kun intends to make a very rich broth.</i>

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:43.670
<i>To counter that, should I also make broth with an equally strong flavor?</i>

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.530
First things first. I have to start testing!

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:50.480
<i>It's no good!</i>

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:54.990
<i>When I try to make a rich broth, 
the flavors don't come together.</i>

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:56.710
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.170
Megumi!

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:01.420
You have a package from your home.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:02.720
What?

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:05.740
<i>Megumi,</i>

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:09.570
<i>congratulations on proceeding to the main tournament of the Autumn Elections.</i>

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:12.130
<i>Though I can't come cheer 
you on because of work,</i>

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:13.340
<i>I wish you the best of luck.</i>

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.960
<i>I'm sending you ingredients from home.</i>

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.190
Mom...

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:22.700
<i>Wow, all of this brings back memories.</i>

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:25.750
<i>So many ingredients 
I used to cook with back home!</i>

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:33.250
<i>I'll use the ingredients 
my mom sent me in the match!</i>

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:38.340
Um...

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.420
That spot's got a weird splashy vibe going on.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.680
Oh, Yukihira, over here!

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:50.640
Why do they write names on fans, Bro?

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:52.180
It's one of Japan's mysteries.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:54.720
Hm...

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:55.970
Ramen.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:07:01.650
It is a dish comprised of three components:
 noodles, toppings, and soup.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:05.360
You just keep the challenging topics coming year after year, don't you?

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.110
Indeed.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:10.890
Ramen enjoyed an explosive popularity after the war, during the recovery period.

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:15.460
The popularity was due to their affordable taste
 and the ease of access, thanks to noodle carts.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:20.840
<i>And now, ramen has become a Japanese cuisine that has gone global.</i>

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:24.090
<i>There's limitless potential for the depth of flavor and amount of effort spent preparing it.</i>

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:26.880
And we're asking contestants to perfect it all in a single night,

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.470
on such a big stage!

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:31.710
In essence, what is being tested in this match

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:33.430
is flexibility and explosive power!

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:38.940
How well can they bring the experience and aptitude that they've nurtured thus far to bear on the topic at hand?

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:43.360
Kurokiba Ryou made seafood 
curry in the preliminaries.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.200
I wonder what he's making 
for the main tournament.

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:50.070
That broth is based on stock taken entirely from fish heads and bones!

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.050
Scorpionfish, conger eel,
 flounder, and red gurnard.

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:54.950
So the ramen will have a seafood broth!

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:56.330
A-ha!

00:07:56.890 --> 00:08:00.420
All the strong flavors of fish guts 
and shrimp innards.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:04.130
It seems he has been able to avoid any fishiness thus far! Well done.

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:07.840
<i>Like I thought, Kurokiba-kun is making a rich broth from seafood.</i>

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:09.050
Scallops!

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:12.760
Megumi is using dried scallops to make her stock.

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:16.180
<i>Add strained paitan soup to the stock...</i>

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:18.390
<i>and simmer the broth!</i>

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:22.340
Wait. So Megumi's also making a seafood broth?

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:25.030
No, they may both be using seafood,

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:28.110
but in contrast to Kurokiba Ryou's rich broth,

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.030
Tadokoro-san chose a light broth.

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:35.160
But can her broth compete against the impact of Kurokiba's rich broth?

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:36.450
Of course it can!

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.430
Megumi's hometown is a harbor town!

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:41.450
I doubt he knows more 
about seafood than she does!

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.500
Very interesting.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.550
Two people who grew up in
 harbor towns against each other.

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:47.630
Right, a fishing port...

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:48.280
What?!

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.450
Nakiri Alice?!

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:52.130
Wh-Why are you here?!

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:53.480
Huh? Am I not allowed?

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:56.140
You said they're both from harbor towns?

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:56.850
That's right!

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:59.770
Ryou-kun grew up next to the sea.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:03.520
A huge pile of lobster 
and sweet shrimp shells?

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.480
Is he going to use them for stock too?

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:15.870
What the hell?!

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:17.660
He's crushing the shells into powder!

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:25.510
There's a place that's popular in the sailors' watering hole district.

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:27.670
Really? I want to check it out.

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:29.880
I'd advise against it!

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:32.460
You'll lose everything you have to a savage!

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.770
Now that I've finally left Japan,

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:41.030
I should try to experience 
lots of different flavors.

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:42.920
This must be the place.

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:45.840
What, a customer?

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:47.400
The place is on break right now.

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:48.120
Get your food somewhere else—

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:50.150
Then I'll just wait inside!

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:52.360
Wow, it's so dirty in here!

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:56.030
I know! Since I'm here,
 can you introduce me to the chef?

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:59.540
You won't get to do as you please here.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:01.660
The chef of this place...

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:03.580
is me.

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:04.860
What?

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:06.010
A chef?

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:07.750
That's right.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:11.480
Ryou-kun has been the head chef 
since he was very young.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.360
That's the kind of chef he is.

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:15.480
M-Megumi's the same way!

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:18.810
She has the experience of helping out at her kitchen back home too!

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:21.540
Megumi!

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:23.190
Don't let any of this get to you!

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:25.690
We've got your back!

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:29.020
What the hell's that?

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:32.650
O-Oh, they're friends from my dorm.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:34.910
I don't like this at all.

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:39.990
I feel sick to my stomach whenever
 I see a bunch of chefs palling around.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:44.500
Chefs are all about winning or being beaten.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.500
There can be nothing else!

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.760
Are you... sure about that?

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:49.970
What?

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:54.680
Isn't it important for people to work together in cooking too?

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.770
The kitchen is a battlefield.

00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:58.340
Cooking is about power!

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:02.470
You wouldn't understand because you were sheltered as a kid.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.720
All your cooking needs to do is to bring your opponents to their knees.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:07.970
That's it.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:12.580
People who don't get that can only make food with weak flavor!

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:14.200
Get that through your thick skull!

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:18.200
The cooking the rest of you have been doing is just trash—a game of pretend.

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:21.490
You're wrong.

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:23.510
What I...

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:26.000
At least, what I've encountered is...

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:28.750
nothing like trash!

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:31.630
<i>The vegetables have been parboiled.</i>

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:34.800
<i>Mix two types of soy sauce together,</i>

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:39.390
<i>then keep the temperature around 80 degrees Celsius to preserve the flavor.</i>

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:40.800
<i>All right!</i>

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:42.810
Good. She's staying calm.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:43.750
Yup.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:46.690
She's getting each task done 
without wasting any time.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:50.150
<i>What determines ramen's flavor is the stock.</i>

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:55.400
<i>There can be no cloudiness in the light broth she chose for her dish.</i>

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:01.700
Beautiful.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:05.280
It shines, and it is crystal clear.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:12.040
Don't say bad things about
 the people who have...

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:15.170
encouraged me!

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:20.350
That was just me... 
trying to say something!

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:27.970
Okay, it's close to the time limit!

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:30.980
Who will finish first?

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:31.930
All right!

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.350
Whoa, what?

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:35.020
Look at the judges...

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:36.400
What's about to start?

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:40.070
Well, watching the chef work
 at the counter in a ramen shop

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:42.280
is one of the pleasures of ramen.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.410
C-Cooking right in front 
of the Devil of Food?

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.280
Hey!

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:51.330
Don't pressure Megumi!

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.410
Don't worry. She's staying calm.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:58.670
It's even more beautiful 
and fragrant up close!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.170
The toppings seem to be mostly vegetables.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:03.130
This looks promising.

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:04.800
I think things are going her way.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:05.340
Yeah.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.260
Okay, Megumi!

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:08.800
Barrel right along to a win!

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:20.150
That's right. That's Ryou-kun right there.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.190
You...

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:23.690
You're not from around here.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:25.570
Don't be so rude!

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:28.530
I have a name—I'm Alice!

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:29.320
Uh-huh.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:30.950
You should tell me your name too!

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.540
Ryou.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:33.750
Ryou?

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.210
What's your family name?

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:36.460
Kurokiba.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.130
Oh, it sounds kind of Japanese.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.420
So. You'd better have money 
to pay for the food.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.670
Of course I do.

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:44.260
That's fine, then.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:45.850
Man, I'm starving.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.340
What should I eat today?

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:49.760
The regulars are showing up.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.140
There's still time until we open for dinner,

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:54.270
but I guess it's okay. Let's do this.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:57.270
<i>What?</i>

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:00.520
<i>He's... changed!</i>

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:01.270
Line up!

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.900
Pay for your meal and follow my orders.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:09.450
If you can do those two things, I'll serve you food.

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:10.700
I'll open up the place!

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:14.950
Too slow!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:19.330
I told you to prioritize prep work
 and stuffing the chicken!

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:23.630
It's because you tried to multitask without
 having the skills to do it that you fall behind!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:25.210
Forget it.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:27.800
You guys can just go take orders from customers!

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.350
I can't stand it anymore!

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:33.310
What's with your attitude?!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:35.680
Don't you dare think you're better than adults!

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.060
Oh, yeah?

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:40.020
Are you saying you can put better food on the table than me?

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:45.780
I can fill your spot just fine 
all by myself if I have to.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:51.450
I'm sorry, Chef.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.790
Here it comes!

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:57.080
It's the best!

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:01.000
I can't leave land without 
having eaten Ryou's food!

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:07.840
Candidate Kurokiba seems to have finished first!

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.300
Hey, what is that?

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:10.760
What's on top?

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:12.510
Wait a minute. Is that rusk?

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:14.260
Go on. Dig in.

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.720
It's Soupe de Poisson Ramen!

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:18.850
Soupe de Poisson...

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:22.560
It's a southern French soup based on stock made from fish heads, bones, and the shells of shellfish.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:25.360
He adapted it into ramen?

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:26.020
First...

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:27.360
let's try the soup.

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:34.990
<i>The innards of shrimp 
and fish form a rich, cohesive taste.</i>

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:38.000
<i>What ferocious flavor!</i>

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:41.670
<i>Allow me to tangle these noodles 
into the soup and try them!</i>

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:45.540
<i>Oh, God!</i>

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.250
<i>It's making me feel faint!</i>

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.840
<i>The umami is so violent!</i>

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:51.720
The toppings consist of three types of cheese,

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.970
rouille made from aioli sauce 
with added chili peppers,

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:57.390
and tempura batter bits acting as crouton stand-ins!

00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:59.770
And there's the rusk we saw earlier!

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:02.940
It's been smeared with Echire butter,
 then toasted golden brown.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.570
<i>I see!</i>

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:13.280
<i>He was crushing dried shells 
containing concentrated flavor!</i>

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:15.280
So you've finally realized what's going on.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:20.950
That crushed powder is everywhere in this ramen,
 from the soup stock to the butter on the rusk!

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:25.290
The umami factors in shrimp are glycine, algine, and proline.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:28.090
Crustaceans have the highest concentration of those factors among all seafood.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:32.930
He pulverized shells containing all that umami and used the powder directly in the dish,

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:35.590
so of course the result is incredibly delicious.

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:40.350
<i>I see.</i>

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.270
<i>It's so flavorful that it's almost violently so.</i>

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:45.480
<i>For this man, having others eat his food...</i>

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:50.230
<i>is like an all-out fistfight.</i>

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:53.990
<i>He's spent his whole life
 making everyone concede defeat.</i>

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:57.700
How long are you gonna keep putting on your airs, old man?

00:16:58.280 --> 00:16:59.330
It's just you and me now.

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:00.790
Very well!

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:12.510
He went bare-chested without posing!

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:14.760
This is a rare occurrence!

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:18.010
You've got some balls forcing me 
to go bare-chested.

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:20.760
I'll give you that.

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.480
Megumi's about to get her dish evaluated,

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:26.980
but the crowd's just so...

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:31.150
Kurokiba wasn't just shaking water out of his noodles earlier.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:35.110
The crowd's heightening interest toward Tadokoro-san's dish,

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:35.610
curiosity,

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:37.070
and the shift in mood...

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:39.660
He shook all that off too.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.290
Megumi can't be having an easy time in all this.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.540
No, not so fast.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:48.500
<i>Imagine that you're separating the noodles from the strainer, and severing the surface tension.</i>

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:51.960
Megumi!

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.970
She's not letting herself get 
overwhelmed by what's going on.

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:56.880
Yes, she's staying focused.

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:59.340
She only sees what she's making.

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:01.970
She reminds me of Yukihira-kun somehow.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:04.980
Here is my dish.

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:06.440
Please have a taste!

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:10.900
<i>Hm, it is an impressive light-broth ramen that is also pleasing to the eye.</i>

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.990
<i>But after having tasted
 Kurokiba Ryou's rich seafood ramen,</i>

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:17.280
<i>how can hers possibly measure up to its impact?</i>

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:23.290
So strong.

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.500
Such powerful umami!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.370
What?

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:27.960
Isn't it supposed to be a light broth?

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:32.040
What is this sweet umami I am
 detecting in the clean flavor?

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:33.710
This combination of ingredients...

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:35.170
It's kozuyu!

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:36.380
Yes!

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.380
This dish used kozuyu as a base.

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:40.890
Finished with the addition of
 paitan soup and a soy sauce mix,

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:42.970
this is my Kozuyu Chicken Soy Sauce Ramen!

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.310
Kozuyu...

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:48.440
Kozuyu is a traditional regional cuisine of Aizu.

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:51.400
It's a celebratory dish made from scallop stock.

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:54.360
So you adapted a regional dish into ramen.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:57.530
With the scallops playing a central role,

00:18:57.530 --> 00:19:02.870
the flavor rests on the solid foundation provided by the paitan soup.

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:08.290
In addition, the kaeshi employs a mix of light soy sauce
 and white soy sauce, which has a pronounced sweetness.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:11.710
It pairs perfectly with kozuyu,
 which is also seasoned with soy sauce!

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:14.540
That still doesn't account for all the umami.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.920
Where is the rest coming from?

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.630
It comes from vegetables.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:20.840
Vegetables?

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:24.640
The shiitake mushrooms, burdock root, and green beans you see in the topping

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.810
were all dried ingredients that were simmered.

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:28.310
I see!

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:30.770
Drying vegetables concentrates their umami!

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:33.560
Their flavor profiles would change completely from before!

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:36.230
All that umami has dissolved into the broth!

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:38.690
I see.

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:41.450
It's Tadokoro's specialty!

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:44.160
<i>The delicate sweetness specific to vegetables!</i>

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:48.870
<i>Who could have foreseen that it could create such a pure yet powerful broth?</i>

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:52.330
<i>I'm so happy that I can't stop smiling!</i>

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:54.540
Oh, before you finish the noodles,

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.000
please try the paste in the small bowl.

00:19:57.460 --> 00:20:00.010
Add as much as you'd like to the broth.

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:04.800
<i>The acidity is eye-opening!</i>

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.930
<i>It brings the flavors together even tighter still!</i>

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:08.640
What <i>is</i> this?!

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:10.640
I combined Aizu chicken meat

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:14.770
with the thinly sliced white part of scallions and pickled plums, along with seasoning.

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:17.650
I thought it'd allow for a fun change of flavor.

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:20.110
<i>It doesn't just change the flavor!</i>

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:22.740
<i>It harmonizes with the kozuyu's delicate flavors</i>

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:25.660
<i>and heightens the sweetness from the vegetables!</i>

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:28.290
Hey, that ramen of yours!

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.410
Let me try it!

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:31.790
O-Okay!

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:33.750
What a surprise!

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:35.790
Even though both dishes are seafood ramen,

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:40.960
she was able to create this much umami,
 despite taking the dish in a completely different direction!

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:45.220
I know I can't possibly create a strong flavor like what you might expect

00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:47.680
from rich seafood or pork bone stock.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:52.680
It requires great expertise, from preventing fishiness to adjusting the flavors.

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:58.400
But I thought I could manage to make a "strong" balanced ramen

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:03.150
if I used kozuyu as a base and emphasized the umami of scallops and vegetables!

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:08.370
You knew I'd make a rich type of ramen, and you deliberately chose this dish to compete with mine.

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:13.620
This match is getting 
interesting, Tadokoro Megumi!

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:18.840
<i>Deep within her slight frame 
burns a quiet determination.</i>

00:21:19.710 --> 00:21:21.710
<i>She did not fear her formidable opponent</i>

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:27.180
<i>and chose to meet him head-on 
in a fierce umami battle!</i>

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:31.010
Try my ramen too!

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:35.230
<i>What an overpowering fragrance
 and umami of the sea!</i>

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:36.980
<i>I can hardly stay standing!</i>

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:40.860
<i>How can... How can you make a ramen like this?!</i>

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:43.440
<i>But I don't want to lose!</i>

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:45.900
<i>What a pitched battle!</i>

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:48.700
<i>Both of them poured their sheer 
willpower into their ramen,</i>

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:52.240
<i>and it has manifested itself as flavor!</i>

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:58.120
Beat her dish to a pulp, Soupe de Poisson!

00:21:58.540 --> 00:22:03.050
My Scallops and Pai Tan have 
the resolve to defeat any foe,

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:04.130
no matter how formidable!

00:22:09.020 --> 00:22:18.980
Scallops, scallops, scallops!

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:19.020
Shrimp, shrimp, shrimp!

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:48.090
An intensely burning desire was born

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:53.930
But not in me, in someone else

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:58.730
Where's the me who believed that

00:22:58.730 --> 00:23:03.860
All one needs is to have hopes and dreams

00:23:03.860 --> 00:23:09.110
Wrapped around something long, my compass was lost

00:23:09.110 --> 00:23:14.870
On the border of life and death, snow drops bloom

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:20.210
If by some mistake they get smashed

00:23:20.210 --> 00:23:25.380
At least put flowers on the empty husk

00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:31.050
Is that the way things are? Yes, it is

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:36.100
You can call it resignation if you want

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:42.020
But that's not me, that's not me

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:46.650
There's no value in something just anyone could make

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:53.240
The director's taken up the brush!

00:23:53.240 --> 00:23:54.120
Who will be the victor?

00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:55.580
Which one will it be?!

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:10.010
Next episode: "The Generation of Prodigies."
